Z||000004||Bruce||09-06-99||03:58 PM||||The insurance rate is, basically, the same as any other passenger car. I wasn't charged "sports car" rates and I live in Calif., where the incentative to make a buck is quite high. Of course, the final rate would be based on your age and driving record. But, again, the Fiero isn't classified as an exotic car.
Z||000005||Bruce||09-06-99||03:59 PM||||Unless, of course, it has 5 cylinders!!
Z||000006||Cooter||09-06-99||04:41 PM||||When I first got car insurance, the agent explained to me that my liability coverage was coverage on me, the passengers and the other guys vehicle- not my vehicle- and it did not matter what I drove because liability costs the same, depending on drivers age and record etc. . . So far, he has been right. The insurance on my Honda, my Fiero and the 'Burb are all pretty much the same. The weird thing is that the Honda Civic Si is considered a sport/compact but the Fiero is not. But it doesn't matter with liability. The only one that is higher is the wife's car- because we have full coverage on it.
Z||000007||theogre||09-06-99||05:03 PM||||obviously a huge amount of what you pay depends on where you live......<p>I add comp & colision to mine.... It cost me like an extra 10$us.
